<title>INDIA: India's Corporation Bank 96/97 net up 19.5 pct.</title>
<headline>India's Corporation Bank 96/97 net up 19.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net Profit		   1,251.3  vs  1,047.5</p>
<p>    Share (in rupees)	     15.26 vs	9.35</p>
<p>    Total income		 9,397.2  vs  7,753.0</p>
<p>    Interest costs	     5,111.4  vs  4,072.6</p>
<p>    Provision for tax	    830.0  vs    N.A.</p>
<p>    Interest spread	    3,169.8  vs  2,583.4</p>
<p>    Deposits		    66,732.9  vs 57,339.6</p>
<p>    Advances		    30,147.5  vs 24,421.1</p>
<p>    Capital			  820.0  vs  1,120.0</p>
<p>    Capital adqequancy (in pct) 11.3  vs     11.3</p>
<p>Note : The state-run Corporations Bank said it returned capital of 300 million rupees with interest of 59.4 million to the federal governemnt during 1996/97.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91-22-285 2851)</p>
</text>
